  "system_description": {
    "narrative_title": "AI infrastructure arms race and political backlash",
    "narrative_summary": "The dominant narrative is a rapid, capital‑intensive buildout of AI infrastructure (data centres, chips, cloud deals, acquisitions and specialised software) that is reshaping markets, corporate strategy and geopolitics while provoking regulatory, community and national‑security pushback. As an open system it circulates flows of capital, compute capacity, talent, data and regulatory signals across firm, regional and national boundaries; outputs include deployed AI services, concentrated economic power, and social dislocation. Key feedbacks include investment → infrastructure build → local/community resistance → permitting and policy constraints (which can slow or redirect investment), and model/performance advances → new commercial demand → more investment. Systemic vulnerabilities (cybersecurity gaps, financial‑system exposure, supply‑chain chokepoints, and biothreat misuse concerns) create second‑order effects that feed back into policy coordination and private‑sector defensive M&A.",
    "scope": "Inside: data centre construction and siting, chip and cooling infrastructure, corporate cloud and AI contracts, major AI M&A (e.g., Nvidia/Hugging Face), national industrial policy and G20 tech/finance coordination, cybersecurity and biorisk debates, workforce displacement and retraining dynamics, local permitting and public opinion.",
    "super_system": "Global political‑economic technology system (the global digital economy and geopolitics where technological capability, trade policy, capital flows and national security interact).",
    "adjacent_subsystems": [
      "Local land‑use and community politics (permitting, NIMBY, property impacts)",
      "Financial system and market stability (banks, investors, systemic risk)",
      "National security and cybersecurity/biosecurity apparatus",
      "Labor/education and sectoral employment (retraining, occupational shifts)"
    ],
    "evidence_headlines": [
      "National data centre projects are consolidating America’s AI lead",
      "Nvidia to buy Hugging Face for $13 billion in big bet on open AI models - reuters.com",
      "Texas Republicans turn against data centers, putting big tech on notice - reuters.com",
      "Andrew Bailey warns G20 of danger AI poses to financial system",
      "Palo Alto CEO says $1 trillion of cybersecurity infrastructure isn’t ready for AI",
      "Pa. Gov. Shapiro says too many data center developers 'don't care about our communities'"
    ]
  },
